Megataur was the royal fighting Titan of the royal family of [[Sutos Island]]. After Megataur's Seeker, [[Zan-Sutos]], was killed, his Amulet was hidden away by the royal [[Governor of Sutos|Governor]], not wanting the Titan to fall in to the wrong hands. {{source|Like Father Unlike Son}}

Upon [[Grier|Grier's]] return to Sutos with [[the Organization]] backing him to restore order to the island, the Governor bestowed Megataur's Amulet to Grier as the son of the true king of Sutos. Being of noble blood and intentions, Grier was able to bond with Megataur. Grier later invoked him to attack [[Dante Vale|Dante Vale's]] [[Caliban]] and was later seen fighting Dante's [[Metagolem]]. Megataur was invoked again alongside [[Breaker]] against Caliban and Metagolem when Grier and Dante prepared to fight to the end. The battle was averted when Grier revealed his true motive for taking over Sutos was his father, and that he was actually bringing peace to an island plagued with war. Having resolved their differences, Grier allowed Dante and his team to leave. {{source|Like Father, Unlike Son}}

Grier invoked Megataur in [[the Professor's castle]] to fight alongside [[Lok|Lok Lambert's]] [[Baselaird|Powerbonded Baselaird]] whilst helping Dante's team recover a file on [[Rassimov]]. Megataur fought [[Hoffman|Hoffman's]] [[Doberman]] and two [[Undergolem]] Titans summoned by [[Eathon the dog]]. After a fierce battle, Megataur was defeated by one of the Undergolems. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}
